# lionsfundraising.com, the ERP
#
# Rules apply from this file's directory down, so the paths below are relative
# to the hosting account root and match the paths on the server exactly.
#
# The repository is the deploy image. If something must not sit on the live
# host, it must not be tracked here either, and if something is tracked it is
# expected to be uploaded.

# Server generated, regenerated nightly by the host
awstats/

# Rotated archives and application logs. These carry participant names, email
# addresses, phone numbers and IP addresses and must never enter version
# control.
#
# Log directories are excluded by their CONTENTS rather than as directories.
# Excluding a directory makes Git refuse to descend into it, and a negation for
# a file inside can then never match. That is how public_html/logs/.htaccess,
# the deny rule protecting roughly 700KB of session and audit logs, stayed out
# of version control after being created on the server in July 2026.
**/logs/*
!**/logs/.htaccess
*.log

# Access rules are deployable source and are never ignored, wherever they sit.
!**/.htaccess

# Credentials. Nothing containing a key belongs in the repository. The Brevo
# key lives above the docroot and is required in, never inlined.
.env
**/.env
service-account.json
**/service-account.json
.htpasswd

# Archives and scratch
*.zip
**/tmp/rate-limits/
_to_delete/

# Local environment
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~

# Submission records written by the application
**/holdharmless/submissions.log
**/holdharmless/agreements.log
**/hfc/orders.log

# Retired copies kept on disk for reference, never deployed
lionsfundraising_BAK/

# Credentials file at the account root. Never committed.
lions-secrets.php
